    37→---
    39→## Install
    …
    41→```sh
    42→npm install p-queue
    43→```
    45→**Warning:** This package is native [ESM](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Modules) and no longer provides a CommonJS export. If your project uses CommonJS, you'll have to [convert to ESM](https://gist.github.com/sindresorhus/a39789f98801d908bbc7ff3ecc99d99c). Please don't open issues for questions regarding CommonJS / ESM.
    47→## Usage
    …
    49→Here we run only one promise at a time. For example, set `concurrency` to 4 to run four promises at the same time.
    51→```js
    52→import PQueue from 'p-queue';
    53→import got from 'got';
    55→const queue = new PQueue({concurrency: 1});
    57→(async () => {
    58→	await queue.add(() => got('https://sindresorhus.com'));
    59→	console.log('Done: sindresorhus.com');
    60→})();
    62→(async () => {
    63→	await queue.add(() => got('https://avajs.dev'));
    64→	console.log('Done: avajs.dev');
    65→})();
    66→```
    68→## API
    …
    70→### PQueue(options?)
    …
    72→Returns a new `queue` instance, which is an [`EventEmitter3`](https://github.com/primus/eventemitter3) subclass.
    162→### queue
    …
    164→`PQueue` instance.
    236→#### .addAll(fns, options?)
    238→Same as `.add()`, but accepts an array of sync or async functions and returns a promise that resolves when all functions are resolved.
    240→#### .pause()
    242→Put queue execution on hold.
    244→#### .start()
    246→Start (or resume) executing enqueued tasks within concurrency limit. No need to call this if queue is not paused (via `options.autoStart = false` or by `.pause()` method.)
    248→Returns `this` (the instance).
    355→#### .size
    357→Size of the queue, the number of queued items waiting to run.
    419→#### .pending
    421→Number of running items (no longer in the queue).
    440→#### [.concurrency](#concurrency)
    442→#### .isPaused
    444→Whether the queue is currently paused.
    446→#### .isRateLimited
    448→Whether the queue is currently rate-limited due to `intervalCap`. Returns `true` when the number of tasks executed in the current interval has reached the `intervalCap` and there are still tasks waiting to be processed.
